      "value": "<p><em>A battered, swamp-swollen copy of</em> Volo's Guide to Monsters<em>, its spine broken to fall open at the chapter on hags. The margins of that chapter are dense with annotation in three distinct hands — spidery, blocky, and small — trading the same verdict line after line:</em></p><p>\"wrong.\"  \"wrong.\"  \"WRONG.\"</p><p><em>And once, beside a passage on the unbreakable bond of a coven of three, in the smallest of the three hands:</em></p><p>\"…fair.\"</p>",
